cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Faster Flow Simulations: multigrid and single precision for the pressure solve in OpenFOAM"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chawda
    given-names: Shubh
    affiliation: "University of Manchester"
date-released: 2026-07-30
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/shubh-chawda/faster-flow-simulations"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - OpenFOAM
  - multigrid
  - GAMG
  - mixed precision
  - single precision
  - pressure Poisson equation
abstract: >-
  Measurements of two ways to cut the cost of the pressure solve in incompressible
  CFD, on a validated 2D laminar channel in OpenFOAM v2512: algebraic multigrid
  (GAMG), which brings cost growth from n^1.51 down to n^1.22, and single-precision
  arithmetic, which matches double precision in accuracy and saves 14-28% memory but
  whose speed effect reverses with mesh size because its pressure-residual floor
  grows as sqrt(N).
